V8 inspector: describing an error runs none of the page's code.

When a CDP client has Runtime enabled, every error a page logs is
described for it: its name, message and stack, and a preview of its
properties. Reading the stack through V8's own accessor formats a stack
nothing has read yet, and formatting calls the page's
Error.prepareStackTrace; reading the name called a getter the page put on
the error's prototype. A page could tell from those calls that a debugger
was attached (bot detectors check exactly this, and Chrome and Electron
show it too). A debugger that watches must not change what it watches:
the description and the preview now take the stack V8 alone formats,
without keeping it, and the name lookup stops at a getter of the page's
anywhere on the prototype chain.

